{"resource":{"id":"go-beginner-guide","title":"Go — Beginner Guide","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"17 min","pages":20,"lastUpdated":"May 2026","tags":["Programming","Go","Concurrency"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"A friendly, zero-to-first-program walkthrough of Go — syntax, packages, and a first taste of goroutines, explained without jargon."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. Introduction to Go"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Installing Go"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Go Workspace"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. Variables"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Data Types"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. Operators"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. Control Statements"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. Functions"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. Arrays"},{"id":"s10","label":"10. Slices"},{"id":"s11","label":"11. Maps"},{"id":"s12","label":"12. Structs"},{"id":"s13","label":"13. Interfaces"},{"id":"s14","label":"14. Basic Concurrency"},{"id":"s15","label":"15. Summary"},{"id":"review","label":"Beginner Review"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"glossary","label":"Glossary"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Go — Complete Tutorial","tag":"Programming","time":"55 min"},{"title":"Go — Step-by-Step Learning Guide","tag":"Programming","time":"27 min"},{"title":"Go — Cheat Sheet","tag":"Programming","time":"5 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Understand what Go is, why it exists, and where it fits in the industry.</li>\n          <li>Read and write basic Go syntax with confidence.</li>\n          <li>Use variables, types, functions, and control flow correctly.</li>\n          <li>Organize code with packages and modules.</li>\n          <li>Take your first look at goroutines and channels.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. Introduction to Go</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Go (or Golang) is an open-source programming language designed at Google in 2007 by Robert Griesemer, Rob Pike, and Ken Thompson. It compiles to a single static binary, starts almost instantly, and treats concurrency as a first-class feature.</p>\n        <p>Its philosophy: simple syntax, one obvious way to do things, and pragmatic tooling (formatter, linter, tests, race detector — all built-in).</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Go compiles to a single static binary, which makes deployments simple across servers and containers.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Installing Go</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Download the installer from <em>go.dev/dl</em>, run it, then verify:</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>$ go version\ngo version go1.22.0 darwin/arm64</code></pre></div>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5\"/><path d=\"M9 18h6\"/><path d=\"M10 22h4\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Editor tip</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Install the official Go extension for VS Code — it wires up formatting, testing, and the language server automatically.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Go Workspace</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Every project is a <strong>module</strong>. Create one with <code>go mod init example.com/hello</code>. Your <code>go.mod</code> file lists dependencies; <code>go.sum</code> pins their hashes.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>// main.go\npackage main\n\nimport &quot;fmt&quot;\n\nfunc main() {\n  fmt.Println(&quot;Hello, Go!&quot;)\n}</code></pre></div>\n        <p>Run with <code>go run .</code> or build a binary with <code>go build</code>.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Variables</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>var name string = &quot;Ada&quot;\nage := 30 // short declaration, type inferred\nconst Pi = 3.14</code></pre></div>\n        <p>Unused variables are a compile error — Go keeps your code tidy by force.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Data Types</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr class=\"border-b\"><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Category</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Types</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Numeric</td><td class=\"p-2\">int, int64, float64, complex128</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Text</td><td class=\"p-2\">string, rune, byte</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Boolean</td><td class=\"p-2\">bool</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"p-2\">Composite</td><td class=\"p-2\">array, slice, map, struct</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Operators</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Arithmetic (<code>+ - * / %</code>), comparison (<code>== != &lt; &gt;</code>), logical (<code>&amp;&amp; || !</code>). No ternary — use a plain <code>if</code>.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Control Statements</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>if x &gt; 0 {\n  fmt.Println(&quot;positive&quot;)\n} else {\n  fmt.Println(&quot;non-positive&quot;)\n}\n\nfor i := 0; i &lt; 3; i++ { fmt.Println(i) }\n\nswitch day {\ncase &quot;Mon&quot;, &quot;Tue&quot;: fmt.Println(&quot;early week&quot;)\ndefault: fmt.Println(&quot;other&quot;)\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. Functions</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>func add(a, b int) int { return a + b }\n\n// Multiple return values are idiomatic\nfunc divide(a, b float64) (float64, error) {\n  if b == 0 { return 0, fmt.Errorf(&quot;divide by zero&quot;) }\n  return a / b, nil\n}</code></pre></div>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-sky-500/40 bg-sky-500/10 text-sky-900 dark:text-sky-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"M12 16v-4\"/><path d=\"M12 8h.01\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Two return values</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Errors are values in Go — you check them explicitly instead of catching exceptions.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Arrays</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Fixed-size, rarely used directly: <code>var nums [3]int = [3]int{'{'}1,2,3{'}'}</code>. Prefer slices.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Slices</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>nums := []int{1, 2, 3}\nnums = append(nums, 4)\nfmt.Println(len(nums), cap(nums))</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s11\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">11. Maps</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>ages := map[string]int{&quot;Ada&quot;: 30, &quot;Alan&quot;: 41}\nages[&quot;Grace&quot;] = 85\nif v, ok := ages[&quot;Ada&quot;]; ok { fmt.Println(v) }</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s12\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">12. Structs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>type User struct { Name string; Age int }\nu := User{Name: &quot;Ada&quot;, Age: 30}\nfmt.Println(u.Name)</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s13\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">13. Interfaces</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>type Greeter interface { Greet() string }\ntype EN struct{}\nfunc (EN) Greet() string { return &quot;Hello&quot; }</code></pre></div>\n        <p>Interfaces in Go are satisfied <em>implicitly</em> — no <code>implements</code> keyword.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s14\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">14. Basic Concurrency</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>go sayHi()             // launches a goroutine\nch := make(chan int)   // channel for communication\ngo func() { ch &lt;- 42 }()\nfmt.Println(&lt;-ch)      // receives 42</code></pre></div>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1517694712202-14dd9538aa97?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Goroutines are cheap, user-space threads coordinated with channels — Go's signature feature.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s15\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">15. Summary</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>You've now seen every fundamental building block of Go. The rest is practice: read the standard library, ship small tools, and lean on <code>go doc</code> and <code>gofmt</code>.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"review\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Beginner Review</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold\">Chapter Summary</h3>\n        <p>Go emphasises simplicity, static typing, fast compilation, and built-in concurrency.</p>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Key Takeaways</h3>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Every project is a module; every file lives in a package.</li>\n          <li>Errors are values — check them.</li>\n          <li>Slices, maps, and structs cover 90% of your data.</li>\n          <li>Goroutines + channels are how you scale.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Self Assessment</h3>\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>What's the difference between an array and a slice?</li>\n          <li>Why does Go reject unused imports?</li>\n          <li>How do you declare and satisfy an interface?</li>\n        </ol>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Practice Questions</h3>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Write a program that counts word frequencies from stdin.</li>\n          <li>Create a struct <code>Book</code> and a slice of books; sort by year.</li>\n          <li>Launch three goroutines that print 1..5 concurrently.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Is Go hard for beginners?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">No — the syntax is intentionally small. Most people are productive within a week.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Do I need to know C first?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">No, but knowing any typed language helps.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>What editor should I use?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">VS Code or GoLand — both are excellent.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"glossary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Glossary</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>Goroutine</strong> — a lightweight thread managed by the Go runtime.</li>\n          <li><strong>Channel</strong> — a typed pipe for communicating between goroutines.</li>\n          <li><strong>Module</strong> — a versioned collection of packages defined by <code>go.mod</code>.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">\n          Educational content compiled from official Go documentation and community resources.\n          Language features and tooling evolve — always consult go.dev for the latest information.\n          Trademarks belong to their respective owners.\n        </p>\n      </div></section>"}